    {
      "kind": "TextBox",
      "id": 799,
      "name": "Textfeld",
      "x": 713.2766696751519,
      "y": 699.347175117687,
      "px": 220,
      "py": 120,
      "panelOpen": false,
      "text": "# Internet Demo — A Simplified Simulated Internet\n\n  ## Features\n  **Backbone:** Routers BB1–BB5 — eBGP mesh (AS65100–65104)\n  **ISPs:** ISP-Alpha (AS65001), ISP-Beta (AS65002), ISP-Gamma (AS65003) — BGP-peered with the backbone\n  **Home networks:** 4 home routers with DHCP, Wi-Fi SSIDs, and NAT — laptops connect wirelessly\n  **Data centers:** DC-Alpha (www.example.com), DC-Beta (www.betanet.de + e-mail), DC-Gamma (DNS ns1/ns2)\n  **Dual stack:** Backbone, ISPs, and servers are fully IPv4/IPv6 dual-stack — home routers obtain\n  an IPv6 prefix via DHCPv6-PD; home clients configure themselves via SLAAC\n\n  ## Try it out\n  Start the simulation and wait for the routing protocols to converge (~10 seconds)\n  **Ping:** Open a terminal on a home PC → ping www.example.com\n  **Website:** Open a website: www.example.com\n",
      "showTitle": false
    },
